      { id: 6, type: "mcq", q: `In the standard trust game, the amount the investor sends is:`, opts: [`A) doubled`, `B) tripled`, `C) halved`, `D) returned unchanged`], answer: `B`, explanation: `'The amount sent is tripled, creating potential gains from cooperation'.` },
      { id: 7, type: "mcq", q: `Kosfeld et al.'s 2005 study found that intranasal oxytocin increased investor transfers by:`, opts: [`A) 44%`, `B) 20%`, `C) 60%`, `D) 5%`], answer: `A`, explanation: `Oxytocin 'increased investor transfers by 44% compared to placebo'.` },
      { id: 8, type: "mcq", q: `Damage to the ventromedial prefrontal cortex tends to:`, opts: [`A) increase trust`, `B) have no effect`, `C) improve reputation tracking`, `D) reduce trust and investment`], answer: `D`, explanation: `'Patients with VMPFC lesions make fewer investments', so damage reduces trust.` },
      { id: 9, type: "mcq", q: `According to Xiang et al. (2016), when players could see a trustee's past behaviour, they recruited the DLPFC and the:`, opts: [`A) caudate nucleus`, `B) anterior insula`, `C) temporoparietal junction`, `D) amygdala`], answer: `C`, explanation: `Investors 'recruited DLPFC and temporoparietal junction to compute reputation scores'.` },
      { id: 10, type: "sentence_completion", q: `Complete the sentence.`, sentenceTemplate: `Oxytocin's tendency to boost in-group but not out-group trust is termed ___.`, answer: `parochial altruism`, explanation: `This in-group/out-group effect is labelled 'parochial altruism'.` },
      { id: 11, type: "sentence_completion", q: `Complete the sentence.`, sentenceTemplate: `On online platforms, a one-star rating reduces seller revenue by ___.`, answer: `30%`, acceptedAnswers: [`30 per cent`], explanation: `'A one-star rating reduces seller revenue by 30%'.` },
      { id: 12, type: "short_answer", q: `What experimental paradigm is used to study trust in neuroeconomics?`, answer: `the trust game`, acceptedAnswers: [`trust game`], explanation: `'The trust game, a standard experimental paradigm', is used.` },
      { id: 13, type: "short_answer", q: `Which theory underlies efforts to rebuild trust through structured positive interactions?`, answer: `contact theory`, acceptedAnswers: [`contact`], explanation: `Interventions 'incorporate contact theory – structured, repeated positive interactions'.` }
